# Litestream sync drill — 2026-10-19 (A2 fix evidence, local)

Purpose: prove the fix for docs/audit-2026-10-19.md A2 locally before any
live micro2 change. A database created after scripts/install-litestream.sh
rendered /etc/litestream.yml was never replicated (litestream reads its
config at startup only), and snapshot-set freshness could still report it
fresh. Fix: scripts/litestream-sync.sh re-renders the config from
`dg list` (apply = atomic replace + sidecar restart only on change;
--check = per-database coverage report), run every 5 minutes by
deploy/dg-litestream-sync.timer; scripts/host-audit.sh gained a
litestream_coverage probe check.

## Local drill (scripts/litestream-sync-drill.sh), run twice, both PASS

Disposable sandbox: dg serve on 127.0.0.1:17432, file:// replica per
database (bucket stand-in), pinned litestream 0.5.17 (PATH v0.3.13
refused by the drill). Restore is judged on restored row values +
integrity_check, not exit code (docs/backup-compatibility.md finding 1).

Run output (identical shape both runs):

  [litestream-sync-drill] sandbox: /tmp/dg-sync-drill-XXXXXX (server http://127.0.0.1:17432, litestream 0.5.17)
  [litestream-sync-drill] 1 ok: drill_one created, synced, replicating
  [litestream-sync-drill] 2a ok: gap is visible (--check fails, names drill_two)
  [litestream-sync-drill] 2b ok: drill_two replicated after sync (sidecar restarted onto new config)
  restored rows exact + integrity ok
  [litestream-sync-drill] 3 ok: drill_two restored from replica with exact rows
  [litestream-sync-drill] 4 ok: delete removes drill_one from the config on the next sync
  [litestream-sync-drill] PASS: create -> visible gap -> sync -> replicated -> restored exactly; delete -> unregistered

What each step proves:
1. Baseline: first database + first sync replicates (replica LTX present).
2. THE A2 MOMENT: drill_two is created while the sidecar is already
   running. Before sync, --check exits 1 naming drill_two state=missing
   (the gap is now visible instead of silent). After sync apply, the
   sidecar has restarted onto the re-rendered config and drill_two's
   replica contains LTX data.
3. drill_two's local files are deleted; `litestream restore` from the
   replica alone returns rows [(1,alpha),(2,bravo),(3,charlie)] exactly,
   integrity_check ok.
4. `dg delete drill_one --confirm drill_one` + one sync removes
   drill_one from the config; --check passes (delete unregisters).

Unit-level checks of the sync script (stub dg): --print/--check/apply/
no-op/remove all behave; a failing restart command rolls the previous
config back and exits 1 (so the next sync retries instead of the file
claiming coverage the daemon does not have); S3-mode render substitutes
bucket/endpoint/region and leaves credential keys as ${LITESTREAM_S3_*}
references -- the secret value never enters the config.

