## Live install + live drill on micro2 — 2026-10-19 (owner-approved)

scripts/install-litestream.sh ran on micro2 (idempotent second run:
"[litestream-sync] in sync (2 database(s)); no change"). It installed
/usr/local/bin/litestream-sync.sh + dg-litestream-sync.{service,timer},
re-rendered /etc/litestream.yml via the sync script (same 2 databases,
sidecar not restarted -- no coverage change), and the only-copy check
printed "only-copy verified: /etc/dg/litestream.env". One pre-existing
installer bug was found and fixed on the way: step 3b's `python3 -c
'<multiline>'` over ssh never survived ssh argv-joining (the remote
shell executed the Python lines); the program now streams via stdin
(`python3 -`), plus a missing `import sys`.

dg-litestream-sync.timer enabled (5-minute cadence). Live drill, no
manual sync trigger at any point:

1. `dg create a2_scratch` + one marker row. Immediately afterwards,
   `litestream-sync.sh --check` on the host exited 1:
   "litestream-coverage db=a2_scratch state=missing" -- the A2 gap,
   now visible instead of silent.
2. The timer closed it on its own: a2_scratch appeared in
   /etc/litestream.yml within ~90s of polling; --check passed with
   all three databases covered; `litestream status` showed
   a2_scratch ok (the sidecar restarted onto the re-rendered config).
3. Bucket proof: `litestream restore` of a2_scratch on the host
   returned [(1, 'a2-live-marker')] exactly, integrity_check ok,
   first attempt.
4. `dg delete a2_scratch --confirm a2_scratch`: the timer removed it
   from the config within ~170s of polling; --check passes,
   litestream status back to the original 2 databases, both ok.
5. Final DG_AUDIT_TARGET=micro2 scripts/host-audit.sh: verdict pass,
   litestream_coverage {"status":"pass","covered":2}.

Residue, disclosed: the a2_scratch/ replica prefix (a few KB of LTX
from one scratch row) remains in the bucket. There is no boto3/aws CLI
on micro2, and deleting it from the workstation would mean copying the
production secret off the host, which the only-copy rule forbids. It
ages out under bucket lifecycle policy (retention policy itself is A5).
